Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: preserve the input timestamp origin for VC-1

VC-1's startup alignment subtracts the first decoded timestamp. After a
positioned flush this rebases a positive presentation epoch to zero, so the
session's seek mark-in can discard all remaining video as preroll. Keep the
existing alignment relative to the first input timestamp when it is positive.

Leave zero, unknown and negative-preroll startup behavior, sparse timestamp
cadence repair, other codecs and flush state unchanged. Use the existing
FFmpeg saturating subtraction helper for the signed offset arithmetic; this
does not establish a presentation contract for unrepresentable timestamps.

The private public-MFT comparison decodes the same fifteen VC-1 packets at
zero and at +25 seconds after Flush. Both versions produce all thirty native
pixel-exact images; the old version repeats zero-origin timestamps, while
this change preserves the complete +25-second sequence. The original long
VC-1 MediaEngine forward/backward and three-cycle tail seek oracles also pass
with this exact source prototype and the separate 0055 EOS component.
This is not a claim of stall-free playback, all VC-1 profiles or VR parity.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
 
 #include <stdbool.h>
 #include <inttypes.h>
+#include <libavutil/common.h>
 #include <libavutil/imgutils.h>
 #include <libavutil/samplefmt.h>
 #include <libswscale/swscale.h>
@@ -560,10 +561,17 @@
     if (t->avctx->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_VC1)
     {
         if (t->last_video_pts == INT64_MIN && t->video_pts_offset == INT64_MIN)
+        {
             t->video_pts_offset = video_pts;
+            /* A decoder flush does not make a positioned presentation start at
+             * zero. Keep the existing startup alignment relative to the first
+             * input timestamp, including preroll before the requested seek. */
+            if (t->video_input_anchor_pts > 0)
+                t->video_pts_offset = av_sat_sub64( video_pts, t->video_input_anchor_pts );
+        }
 
         if (t->video_pts_offset != INT64_MIN && video_pts >= t->video_pts_offset)
-            video_pts -= t->video_pts_offset;
+            video_pts = av_sat_sub64( video_pts, t->video_pts_offset );
     }
 
     *pts = video_pts;
